think Eleven consecutive push attempts against xy were rejected in a row while eight peer commits landed in the window (shastra's Bhagavat, Paramatma, Krsna, Bhakti, and Priti Sandarbha files plus their send-confirmed logs, and docs-geode's Tattva Sandarbha door sweep). Resolving the Git nib conflict and re-deriving it on every single rebase kept losing the race to the next peer push.
think Broke the cycle by skipping the nib rewrite and page regeneration for one rebase cycle -- accepting the post-commit hook's own advisory that unrefreshed debts may wait for the next commit -- and pushing the bare content change alone. That attempt landed clean at bbec1416a.
think Regenerated readme_metrics.rish and geode_libraries.rish once the push had landed (both wrote byte-identical output), then wrote the Git nib as a follow-up shape naming bbec1416a, committed, and pushed a second time -- also clean, at fb291aefe.
obs The lesson matches remember-git-nib.md's own acknowledged "contested send" edge: chasing a perfectly fresh nib on every intermediate rebase costs more than it buys when the pier is this hot, since each amend-and-repush cycle takes longer than the interval between peer pushes. Landing the content first and carrying the nib forward as a follow-up once the race is won is the cheaper path, and the rule already names this as lawful.
obs Pheromone's own lane stayed idle throughout -- no language-lane build was agent-doable, matching the eleventh idle check's conclusion. This round's entire contribution was staying current with the pier's traffic.
file construction/ITINERARY.md why the Git nib field was rewritten twice more, first left stale through one rebase, then carried forward as a follow-up once the push landed
recommend check in (either) -- same standing ask as the eleventh idle check: pheromone's lane wants either fresh language-lane work or a widened check cadence. Also worth a hand's notice: eleven contested pushes in roughly six minutes is unusually hot traffic even for this pier tonight.
scope this lap: eleven rebase/push cycles against xy, two successful pushes, one mirror to debrided each; no pheromone-lane code built
